  "slides": [
    {
      "page_title": "Objects Without Classes",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Delegation, Not Copying",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "JS has no classical inheritance at runtime",
            "Objects delegate lookups to other objects",
            "`class` is syntax over that delegation"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "A prototype is an ordinary object that another object links to for failed property lookups. Nothing magic, nothing special-cased."
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "const a = { x: 1 }",
            "const b = Object.create(a)  // b links to a",
            "a.x = 99",
            "b.x   // 99 — live link, not a copy"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Link vs Copy"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Operation",
            "Result",
            "Later a.x"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Object.create(a)",
              "linked",
              "visible"
            ],
            [
              "{ ...a }",
              "copied",
              "ignored"
            ],
            [
              "Object.assign({},a)",
              "copied",
              "ignored"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The [[Prototype]] Slot"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Every object has internal slot `[[Prototype]]`",
            "`Object.getPrototypeOf` is the standard accessor",
            "`__proto__` is the legacy accessor, same slot"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "What You Get For Free"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Value",
            "[[Prototype]]",
            "Inherited"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`{}`",
              "Object.prototype",
              "toString"
            ],
            [
              "`[]`",
              "Array.prototype",
              "map, filter"
            ],
            [
              "`function(){}`",
              "Function.prototype",
              "call, bind"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`[].map` is inherited, never an own property",
            "`hasOwnProperty` and `valueOf` come from the root",
            "Object literals get Object.prototype by default"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Null-Prototype Dictionaries"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "const dict = Object.create(null)",
            "dict.a = 1",
            "'toString' in dict   // false — empty chain",
            "dict.toString()      // TypeError: not a fn"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Own vs Inherited",
          "items": [
            "`Object.hasOwn(o,'k')` — own only",
            "`o.hasOwnProperty('k')` — own only",
            "`'k' in o` — walks the whole chain"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Why It Is Cheap"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "10,000 instances, one copy of each method",
            "Reads walk a linked list of objects",
            "Writes (usually) do not walk anything"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Objects Without Classes (cont.)",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Read Algorithm",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "own property?",
              "[[Prototype]]",
              "repeat",
              "null",
              "undefined"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A miss yields `undefined`, never a ReferenceError",
            "Each miss walks one more object",
            "Deep chains make failed lookups measurably slower"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "A Real Chain"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "const a = [1]",
            "Object.getPrototypeOf(a)  // Array.prototype",
            "// a -> Array.prototype -> Object.prototype",
            "//   -> null"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Shadowing And Un-Shadowing"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "const p = { greet: 'hi' }",
            "const o = Object.create(p)",
            "o.greet = 'yo'   // own prop hides p.greet",
            "delete o.greet   // reveals 'hi' again"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Writes Are Not Reads"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Inherited k is",
            "o.k = v does"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "plain data prop",
              "creates OWN prop on o"
            ],
            [
              "accessor with setter",
              "calls that setter"
            ],
            [
              "non-writable data",
              "silently fails"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Assignment never mutates the prototype object",
            "Strict mode turns the silent failure into a TypeError"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Receiver Keeps `this`"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "const proto = { who(){ return this.n } }",
            "const o = Object.create(proto)",
            "o.n = 'me'",
            "o.who()   // 'me' — this is o, not proto"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Reading And Writing The Link"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Call",
            "Does",
            "Cost"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "getPrototypeOf(o)",
              "reads link",
              "cheap"
            ],
            [
              "setPrototypeOf(o,p)",
              "writes link",
              "deoptimizes"
            ],
            [
              "Object.create(p)",
              "links at birth",
              "cheap"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Enumeration And Chain Tests"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`for...in`: own AND inherited enumerable string keys",
            "`Object.keys`: own enumerable only",
            "`x instanceof C`: is C.prototype in x's chain?",
            "Cyclic links throw a TypeError on the spot"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Two Words, Two Things",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "",
            "prototype",
            "__proto__"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Lives on",
              "functions only",
              "every object"
            ],
            [
              "Means",
              "future instances' parent",
              "this object's parent"
            ],
            [
              "Use for",
              "`new` wiring",
              "legacy reads"
            ]
          ]
        }
      ],
      "cont": true
    },
    {
      "page_title": "__proto__ vs prototype",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Invariant To Memorize"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "function Dog(){}",
            "const d = new Dog()",
            "Object.getPrototypeOf(d) === Dog.prototype  // ✓",
            "Dog.__proto__ === Function.prototype        // ✓"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`fn.prototype` is NOT fn's own prototype",
            "A function's own prototype is Function.prototype",
            "`Dog.prototype` is only for things `new Dog()` makes"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The constructor Link"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "Dog.prototype.constructor === Dog  // true",
            "Dog.prototype = { bark(){} }       // link gone",
            "Dog.prototype.constructor = Dog    // restore it"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Root Of The Chain"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Expression",
            "Value"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Function.prototype.__proto__",
              "Object.prototype"
            ],
            [
              "Object.prototype.__proto__",
              "null"
            ],
            [
              "Object.create(null).__proto__",
              "plain data key"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Why __proto__ Is Risky"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Annex B legacy accessor on Object.prototype",
            "Web-compat only — prefer the `Object.*` calls",
            "It is a setter: naive merges can write the root",
            "A `\"__proto__\"` key in untrusted JSON is an attack"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "No prototype Property"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Arrow functions have none",
            "Object-literal method shorthand has none",
            "`class` methods have none — none can be `new`ed"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Wiring Diagram"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "instance",
              "Ctor.prototype",
              "Object.prototype",
              "null"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Off To The Side",
          "items": [
            "`Ctor.__proto__` → Function.prototype",
            "Statics live on Ctor itself",
            "Instances never see statics"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Four Steps Of new",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "make {}",
              "link to Fn.prototype",
              "call Fn, this = it",
              "return it"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "__proto__ vs prototype (cont.)",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Step 4 is skipped if the body returns an object",
            "Returning a primitive is ignored entirely"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Return Override Rule"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "function A(){ this.a = 1; return { b: 2 } }",
            "new A()   // { b: 2 } — instance replaced",
            "function B(){ this.a = 1; return 7 }",
            "new B()   // B { a: 1 } — 7 ignored"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Idiomatic Split"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "function Dog(n){ this.name = n }  // per-instance",
            "Dog.prototype.speak = function(){",
            "  return this.name + ' barks'     // shared",
            "}"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Per-instance state in the constructor body",
            "Shared methods on `Fn.prototype`, one copy total"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Forgetting new"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Mode",
            "Dog('rex') gives"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "strict / module",
              "this undefined, TypeError"
            ],
            [
              "sloppy",
              "this = global, silent leak"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "function Dog(n){",
            "  if (!new.target) return new Dog(n)  // guard",
            "  this.name = n",
            "}"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`new.target` is undefined on a plain call",
            "It is the constructor itself on a `new` call"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "ES5 Inheritance By Hand"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "function Child(n){ Parent.call(this, n) }  // up",
            "Child.prototype =",
            "  Object.create(Parent.prototype)",
            "Child.prototype.constructor = Child"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`Child.prototype = new Parent()` is the wrong idiom",
            "It runs the parent constructor far too early",
            "Parent fields leak onto the shared prototype"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Building Without new",
          "items": [
            "`Object.create(proto, descriptors)` calls nothing",
            "Factory: return a literal closing over state",
            "No `this`, no `new` — but one copy per instance"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Call Site Decides",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "In a normal function, `this` is fixed by how the function is called, not by where it was written."
        }
      ],
      "cont": true
    },
    {
      "page_title": "How `this` Gets Its Value",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Four Rules"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Rule",
            "Call",
            "this"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "default",
              "`f()`",
              "undefined (strict)"
            ],
            [
              "implicit",
              "`obj.f()`",
              "obj"
            ],
            [
              "explicit",
              "`f.call(o)`",
              "o"
            ],
            [
              "new",
              "`new F()`",
              "fresh object"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Sloppy-mode default binding gives globalThis",
            "Only the LAST dot counts: `a.b.f()` gives `b`",
            "`bind` is explicit binding made permanent"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Precedence Order"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "new",
              "bind/call/apply",
              "obj.f()",
              "default"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Arrows sit outside this list entirely",
            "They have no `this` of their own to set"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Lost Binding Bug"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "const o = { n: 'o', f(){ return this.n } }",
            "o.f()          // 'o'",
            "const f = o.f  // receiver dropped here",
            "f()            // TypeError — this undefined"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Accessors And Module Tops"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Where",
            "this is"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "getter / setter",
              "the receiver, not definer"
            ],
            [
              "ESM top level",
              "undefined"
            ],
            [
              "CJS top level",
              "module.exports"
            ],
            [
              "classic script",
              "globalThis"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "DOM Handlers"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "el.onclick = function(){ this }  // the element",
            "el.onclick = () => this          // outer this",
            "// safest either way: event.currentTarget"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Two Questions",
          "text": "Is it an arrow? Then look outward. Otherwise: what sits left of the final dot at the call site?"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Three, Side By Side",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Call",
            "When",
            "Arguments"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "fn.call(o,a,b)",
              "now",
              "listed one by one"
            ],
            [
              "fn.apply(o,[a,b])",
              "now",
              "array-like (A for A)"
            ],
            [
              "fn.bind(o,a)",
              "never",
              "partial, new function"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Hard Binding Is Permanent"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "const b = f.bind(o1)",
            "b.call(o2)      // still o1 — rebind ignored",
            "new b()         // this = fresh obj, o1 lost"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`new` DOES override a bound `this`",
            "Bound leading arguments are still prepended",
            "Everything else about the binding is frozen"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "call, apply, and bind",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Listener Trap"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "el.addEventListener('x', fn.bind(o))",
            "el.removeEventListener('x', fn.bind(o))",
            "// different object — removes nothing",
            "const h = fn.bind(o)   // store one reference"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Partial Application"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "function add(a, b){ return a + b }",
            "const add5 = add.bind(null, 5)",
            "add5(3)   // 8"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Method Borrowing"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "[].slice.call(arguments)   // array-ify",
            "[].map.call(nodeList, f)   // any array-like"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "toString.call(x)",
            "Returns"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`[]`",
              "[object Array]"
            ],
            [
              "`null`",
              "[object Null]"
            ],
            [
              "`new Date()`",
              "[object Date]"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Sloppy vs Strict thisArg"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Sloppy: `call(null)` substitutes globalThis",
            "Sloppy: a primitive thisArg gets boxed",
            "Strict: both pass through untouched"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Modern Replacements"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`fn(...args)` instead of `apply`",
            "`Reflect.apply(fn, thisArg, args)` for a clean path",
            "`bind` allocates — keep it out of render loops"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "No Binding At All",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "An arrow has no `this` of its own",
            "`this` resolves lexically, like any other variable",
            "`call`/`apply`/`bind` ignore the thisArg silently"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Callback Fix"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "setTimeout(() => this.tick(), 100)  // works",
            "setTimeout(function(){",
            "  this.tick()                       // broken",
            "}, 100)"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Replaces `const self = this`",
            "Replaces `.bind(this)` wrappers",
            "Replaces the thisArg param of forEach/map"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Also Missing From Arrows"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Inside an arrow",
            "Resolves to"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`arguments`",
              "enclosing function's"
            ],
            [
              "`super`",
              "enclosing method's"
            ],
            [
              "`new.target`",
              "enclosing scope's"
            ],
            [
              "`prototype`",
              "does not exist"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "const A = () => {}",
            "new A()  // TypeError: not a constructor"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Where Arrows Break"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "const o = { name: 'a', get: () => this.name }",
            "o.get()   // undefined — outer this, not o",
            "Dog.prototype.speak = () => this.name // bad"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Arrow Functions and Lexical `this`",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Method shorthand `{ get(){} }` works fine",
            "A prototype arrow can never see the instance",
            "It is broken identically for every instance"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Arrow Class Fields"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "class B { handle = () => this.x }  // bound",
            "// own property per instance, not on prototype"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Auto-binds, at one function per instance",
            "Not on the prototype: `super.handle()` fails",
            "Shadows any same-named prototype method"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Pick By Call Site",
          "text": "Arrow for callbacks and short lexical closures. `function` or method shorthand when the call site should supply `this`."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Still Just A Function",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "class C { m(){} }",
            "typeof C                  // 'function'",
            "C.prototype.m             // method lives here",
            "Object.keys(C.prototype)  // [] — hidden"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Class methods are non-enumerable",
            "So `for...in` over an instance skips them",
            "Hand-written prototype assignment does not hide them"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Where Members Land"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Declaration",
            "Lands on"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`m(){}`",
              "C.prototype"
            ],
            [
              "`static s(){}`",
              "C itself"
            ],
            [
              "`x = 1`",
              "each instance"
            ],
            [
              "`get v(){}`",
              "C.prototype accessor"
            ],
            [
              "`#x = 1`",
              "private slot"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "extends Wires Two Links"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "class Child extends Parent {}",
            "const gp = Object.getPrototypeOf",
            "gp(Child.prototype) === Parent.prototype",
            "gp(Child) === Parent   // static inheritance"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Line 3 is the instance-method link",
            "Line 4 is what manual ES5 patterns forgot",
            "`class` gives you both for free"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "super And this"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`super.m()` uses the method's `[[HomeObject]]`",
            "Not `this.__proto__.m()` — extracted methods still resolve",
            "`super(args)` is what actually CREATES `this`",
            "Touching `this` before it: ReferenceError"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Strictness And Hoisting"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Situation",
            "Result"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "class body code",
              "always strict mode"
